<resources>
    <!--
    SETUP — Release build Google Maps API key
    ==========================================
    This file is a template. Copy it to:
        app/src/release/res/values/google_maps_api.xml
    and replace the placeholder with your real key.

    This key is used ONLY for the Android Maps SDK (map tile rendering).
    Directions API requests are now proxied through the FastAPI backend,
    so this key never makes web-service calls and can be safely restricted.

    RECOMMENDED RESTRICTION (Google Cloud Console)
    -----------------------------------------------
    Restrict this key to "Android apps" and add:
      • Package name:  com.shubham.womensafety
      • SHA-1 fingerprint: get your release keystore SHA-1 with:
          keytool -list -v -keystore your-release-key.jks -alias your-alias

    HOW TO GET A KEY FOR RELEASE
    -----------------------------
    1. Go to https://console.cloud.google.com → APIs & Services → Credentials
    2. Create an API key (or reuse one) with "Maps SDK for Android" enabled
    3. Apply the Android-app restriction with your release keystore SHA-1
    4. Replace the placeholder below with your key (it starts with "AIza")
    -->
    <string name="google_maps_key" templateMergeStrategy="preserve" translatable="false">YOUR_RELEASE_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY</string>
</resources>
